WHY GPL v3
----------
This application embeds the *Repertorium Publicum* repertory dataset inside one
self-contained HTML file.  That dataset is third-party material published under
GPL v3 (see below).  Distributing it as part of a combined work means the
combined work is distributed under GPL v3.

GPL v3 also forbids adding further restrictions on top of it.  No clause in this
file therefore restricts commercial use of the GPL-covered material.

This corrects two errors in earlier versions of this file, which stated that the
repertory text was public domain and that commercial use required a licence.
Both statements contradicted the licence of the embedded data and have been
removed.


THE EMBEDDED DATA
-----------------
    Repertorium Publicum (2008)
    Vladimir Polony — an open, Kent-derived repertory, published as part of the
    OpenRep source code under GPL v3.

    It is NOT Kent's Repertory of the Homoeopathic Materia Medica, 1897 first
    edition.  It has its own chapter structure and its own additions.

    source : https://github.com/nondeterministic/oorep
    licence: GNU General Public License v3

The source of this application — the HTML, the build pipeline and the extracted
data — is this repository, so the corresponding source is available to anyone
who receives a copy.


REQUESTS (not conditions of the licence)
